// Every main-loop entry point (SCOPE) and every diagnostic note (NOTE), one table for the plugin
// and scottland-loop-read. Ids are positions: add new rows anywhere; readers take names from the
// names file of the instance that wrote a record (docs/main-loop.md).
//
// SCOPE(name, kind): kind is work, or diagnostic for the watchdog's own traffic (timed and counted
// toward ML2, but it neither keeps the watchdog at its fast rate nor counts as activity).
// NOTE(name, text): {N} is argument N (1-4) in decimal; {N:x} hex; {N:s} signed; {N:p} an x,y pair
// (two signed 32-bit halves); {N:lo:bits} a bit field; {N:lo:bits:a|b|...} a bit field naming its values.

